# Why DNA pairs A with T and C with G
subtitle: "How the fit of big and small bases makes DNA its own template, so each strand can rebuild the other letter for letter"

## Why DNA pairs A with T and C with G
use: dna_helix
with: {"turns":2,"show_base_pairs":true,"labels":true}
sources:
    - id: wc1953
      title: 'Molecular structure of nucleic acids: a structure for deoxyribose nucleic acid'
      authors: Watson JD, Crick FHC
      year: 1953
      finding: The double helix with A–T and G–C pairing; the closing sentence notes that the pairing suggests a copying mechanism.

